# Never commit the generated environment or operator secrets.
.env
# The cluster manifest is written on a live primary by `./taranac cluster …` and edited
# by the operator (its `skip:` section). It holds no secrets — only topology — but it
# describes ONE deployment, so it must never be committed back into the product.
config/cluster.yml
config/tls/*
!config/tls/.gitkeep
!config/tls/README.md
config/firebase/*
!config/firebase/.gitkeep
!config/firebase/README.md
# HA etcd client-TLS material + the unified cluster secret set (ha.md §7.3/§12) — these
# hold private keys (etcd CA key, server leaves, mfa key). NEVER commit them. But KEEP the
# empty dirs (via .gitkeep) so they ship in the bundle USER-owned — else Docker auto-creates
# config/etcd-tls as ROOT on the first RO mount and the operator can't write leaves (#31).
config/etcd-tls/*
!config/etcd-tls/.gitkeep
config/etcd-ca/*
!config/etcd-ca/.gitkeep
config/cluster-secrets/*
!config/cluster-secrets/.gitkeep
